Z||000000||fiero_nightmare||10-28-2001||11:22 AM||||for a few weeks now i have been trying to decide on what color(s) i am going to paint my 85 GT.i had a hard time deciding between metallic blue W/ silver ground affects,  silverW/gray ground affects,   gray w/silver ground affects,   black with silver/gray ground affects and the factory white with gray ground affects.  <P> <BR>i have decided to go with black with metallic silver ground affects.<P>i will have to wait until spring to paint it and i decided it would be a lot cheaper to go with enamel paint instead of a clearcoat job.<P>how shiny will a enamel paint job be without having it buffed out?<P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <P>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||10-28-2001||11:42 AM||||I would go with a clearcoat paint.  A single stage paint will be shiney but I think you'd be happier with the clear.  The more clear you put on the deeper the paint gets.  I'd save up for the clear!Just my opinion. <P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature2_copy_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||85 gt fiero||10-28-2001||11:46 AM||||Yah,i am painting my 85 gt rally car bright yellow right now i was thinking about painting the ground effects yellow too. if youre talking about the paint that you dont have to put clear coat on it i have painted two forsrangers with that kind of paint its still bright and metalic but it does require a bit of wetsanding afterwards to make it really smooth. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   Randy<P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES AND SOON TO BE BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||1
